zlib 1.3.2 security backports

The zlib-1.3.2-*.patch files are exact fixes from the upstream zlib project,
copyright Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler, under the zlib license. The full
license accompanies built engines in licenses/zlib/LICENSE.

https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/df84af25dc1942490e1d1c899a07619152a46148
Fixes CVE-2026-85091, a buffer overflow after a failed nonblocking write.

https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/e9415f70eb6a37c4b6b9685b12e8e6ac91c80f54
Initializes the input buffer before gzip zero-fill, preventing uninitialized
application memory from being compressed after a forward seek before writing.
